  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "e4c89131-b38c-4843-99b0-c9c451732775",
    "name": "Daring Foods Discovery Metadata API",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": {
      "content": "The metadata layer that makes the whole daring.com surface machine-readable without prior knowledge. `GET /` returns the site identity, the list of registered namespaces (10 on this host) and the full route index (222 routes), along with the `authentication` block advertising WordPress Application Passwords as the credential mechanism for the write side. `/wp/v2/types` enumerates every registered post type - which is how the site's three custom collections (`products`, `foodservice-products`, `recipes`) are discovered - and `/wp/v2/taxonomies` maps each taxonomy to the types it applies to. `/wp/v2/statuses` and `/wp/v2/users` complete the picture. Note that `/wp/v2/settings` requires authentication and returns HTTP 401 anonymously, so it is deliberately not documented here.\n\nContact Support:\n Name: Daring Foods",
      "type": "text/plain"
    }
  }
